  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 73,
  "title": "Psalms 73",
  "display_title": "Psalms 73",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "psalms",
  "book": "Psalms",
  "bookName": "Psalms",
  "bookOrder": 19,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 73,
  "sortOrder": 19073,
  "verseCount": 28,
  "aliases": [
    "Psalm",
    "Psalms",
    "Ps",
    "Psa",
    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Truly God is good to Israel, even to such as are of a clean heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "But as for me, my feet were almost gone; my steps had well nigh slipped.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For I was envious at the foolish, when I saw the prosperity of the wicked.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For there are no bands in their death: but their strength is firm.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "They are not in trouble as other men; neither are they plagued like other men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Therefore pride compasseth them about as a chain; violence covereth them as a garment.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Their eyes stand out with fatness: they have more than heart could wish.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "They are corrupt, and speak wickedly concerning oppression: they speak loftily.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "They set their mouth against the heavens, and their tongue walketh through the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Therefore his people return hither: and waters of a full cup are wrung out to them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "And they say, How doth God know? and is there knowledge in the most High?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Behold, these are the ungodly, who prosper in the world; they increase in riches.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Verily I have cleansed my heart in vain, and washed my hands in innocency.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "For all the day long have I been plagued, and chastened every morning.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "If I say, I will speak thus; behold, I should offend against the generation of thy children.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "When I thought to know this, it was too painful for me;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Until I went into the sanctuary of God; then understood I their end.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Surely thou didst set them in slippery places: thou castedst them down into destruction.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "How are they brought into desolation, as in a moment! they are utterly consumed with terrors.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "As a dream when one awaketh; so, O Lord, when thou awakest, thou shalt despise their image.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Thus my heart was grieved, and I was pricked in my reins.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "So foolish was I, and ignorant: I was as a beast before thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Nevertheless I am continually with thee: thou hast holden me by my right hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Thou shalt guide me with thy counsel, and afterward receive me to glory.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Whom have I in heaven but thee? and there is none upon earth that I desire beside thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "My flesh and my heart faileth: but God is the strength of my heart, and my portion for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "For, lo, they that are far from thee shall perish: thou hast destroyed all them that go a whoring from thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:73:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "But it is good for me to draw near to God: I have put my trust in the Lord GOD, that I may declare all thy works.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 73:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:73:28"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
